      <Desc>Through our schools, we supported the graduation of over 100 Afghan girls at the end of the school year, who completed their high school graduation and received additional certificate achievement for their completion of our rigorous STEM and computer coding programs.We supported the expansion of schools for girls to Daikundi, Herat, and Samangan. Our support provides access to education to over 700 students across our three academies, equipping young women with the skills and confidence to redefine their futures and uplift their communities.</Desc>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
        <ExpenseAmt>3968</ExpenseAmt>
        <RevenueAmt>0</RevenueAmt>
        <Desc>In Athens, Greece 50 students participated in our English and Greek language, and digital literacy classes 50 students participated in our health education classes . 1000+ grocery kits distributed to poor refugees in Central Athens . 110 Afghans connected with jobs and provided job readiness training. 50+ health lessons provided for the community. For Ramadan and food aid in Greece, we provided over 3000 healthy and culturally appropriate meals to refugees in need.</Desc>
      </ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy3Grp>
        <ExpenseAmt>715</ExpenseAmt>
        <RevenueAmt>0</RevenueAmt>
        <Desc>We provided a workshop to educate elected officials and local communities on the impacts of Gender Apartheid in Afghanistan, including a Congressional Briefing on Gender Apartheid, and highlighted issues concerning the rights of women and girls in Afghanistan. As part of our program, we provided holistic group therapy services to over 25 Women HRDs from Afghanistan and in the diaspora who are directly impacted by the situation of women's rights in Afghanistan</Desc>
      </ProgSrvcAccomActy3Grp>
